== Campaign issues ==
{{Missing information|section|the campaign stances of other candidates|date=July 2025}}

=== Campaign themes ===
==== Nawrocki's campaign ====
[[File:02024 1850 Open Meeting with Karol Nawrocki in Bielsko-Biała.jpg|thumb|Anti-Tusk "NIE BAĆ TUSKA" sign at a Nawrocki meeting in [[Bielsko-Biała]]]]
Karol Nawrocki pitted his campaign against the unpopular{{efn|The government and Prime Minister have received net negative approval between January and May 2025, both situated within -2 to -20<ref>{{bulletlist|{{cite news |date={{date|2025-03-26|DMY}} |last=Kwapisz |first=Bartłomiej |title=Połowa Polaków negatywnie ocenia pracę rządu i premiera. Nowy sondaż CBOS |url=https://wydarzenia.interia.pl/kraj/news-polowa-polakow-negatywnie-ocenia-prace-rzadu-i-premiera-nowy,nId,21323415 |access-date=2025-07-12}}|{{cite news |date={{date|2025-04-22|DMY}} |last=Czurczak |first=Aleksandra |title=Polacy ocenili rząd Donalda Tuska. Najnowszy sondaż |url=https://wydarzenia.interia.pl/kraj/news-polacy-ocenili-rzad-donalda-tuska-najnowszy-sondaz,nId,21397042 |access-date=2025-07-12}}|{{cite news |date={{date|2025-05-08|DMY}} |title=Sondaż Atlas Wybory Prezydenckie w Polsce 2025 |url=https://atlasintel.org/poll/poland-national-08-05-2025 |access-date=2025-07-12}}}}</ref> net approval.}} government and Prime Minister, declaring the election as a referendum on the Tusk cabinet,<ref name=referendum/> and attacking Trzaskowski for being the vice-chairman of the ruling [[Civic Platform]].<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-05-24|DMY}} |title="Panie wiceprzewodniczący". Nawrocki w kółko powtarzał jedno określenie |url=https://polskieradio24.pl/artykul/3528042,panie-wiceprzewodniczacy-nawrocki-w-kolko-powtarzal-jedno-okreslenie |access-date=2025-07-13}}</ref> He portrayed himself as a nonpartisan "citizens' candidate" ({{langx|pl|kandydat obywatelski}}) supported by [[Law and Justice]], as he was never a member of any political party,<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-02-27|DMY}} |title=Karol Nawrocki: Kim jest kandydat na prezydenta wspierany przez PiS? |url=https://www.rp.pl/polityka/art41846761-karol-nawrocki-kim-jest-kandydat-na-prezydenta-wspierany-przez-pis |access-date=2025-07-13}}</ref> and as an authentic "flesh and bone man" ({{langx|pl|człowiek z krwi i kości}}), contrasting with Trzaskowski by calling him the product of a political laboratory.<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-04-27|DMY}} |last=Żak |first=Karol |title="Wytwór politycznego laboratorium". Nawrocki uderza w Trzaskowskiego |url=https://www.rmf24.pl/raporty/raport-wybory-prezydenckie-2025/news-wytwor-politycznego-laboratorium-nawrocki-uderza-w-trzaskows,nId,7955910 |access-date=2025-07-13}}</ref> Nawrocki's campaign was oriented around the welfare of citizens, national security and infrastructural development.<ref name=nawrockiprogram>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-05-15|DMY}} |title=Program wyborczy Karola Nawrockiego. Oto szczegóły |url=https://www.pap.pl/aktualnosci/program-wyborczy-karola-nawrockiego-oto-szczegoly |access-date=2025-07-13}}</ref>

==== Trzaskowski's campaign ====
Rafał Trzaskowski defended the incumbent coalition government, blaming its inaction on the presidential veto of incumbent president [[Andrzej Duda]].<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-04-10|DMY}} |last=Strzelińska |first=Karina |title=Gra o ustawy. Co może, a co zrobi nowy prezydent? |url=https://www.gazetaprawna.pl/wiadomosci/artykuly/9774384,gra-o-ustawy-co-moze-a-co-zrobi-nowy-prezydent.html |access-date=2025-07-15}}</ref> He portrayed himself as a competent and educated candidate, highlighting his knowledge of foreign languages, education and political experience,<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-01-30|DMY}} |last=Wielowieyska |first=Dominika |title="Zna pięć języków, ma tytuł doktora i dwa fakultety". Przegięli z tym fejkiem - mówi mi bliska osoba, pokazując w telefonie bio Trzaskowskiego |url=https://wyborcza.pl/magazyn/7,124059,31651823,zna-piec-jezykow-ma-tytul-doktora-i-dwa-fakultety-przegieli.html |archive-url=https://archive.today/20250130065132/https://wyborcza.pl/magazyn/7,124059,31651823,zna-piec-jezykow-ma-tytul-doktora-i-dwa-fakultety-przegieli.html |archive-date={{date|2025-01-30|DMY}} |access-date=2025-07-13}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-05-21|DMY}} |last=Halicki |first=Piotr |title=Poliglota, samorządowiec, kandydat na prezydenta. Kim jest Rafał Trzaskowski? |url=https://wiadomosci.onet.pl/wybory/wybory-prezydenckie/kim-jest-rafal-trzaskowski-sylwetka-kandydata-na-prezydenta/vxc6mhd |access-date=2025-07-13}}</ref> promising to be independent of party decisionmaking.<ref name=trzaskowskiprogram>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-05-15|DMY}} |title=Program wyborczy Trzaskowskiego. Tak wyglądają jego postulaty |url=https://www.pap.pl/aktualnosci/program-wyborczy-trzaskowskiego-tak-wygladaja-jego-postulaty |access-date=2025-07-13}}</ref> He challenged Nawrocki's nonpartisan presentation, attacking him as the "decision of the [PiS] party chairman".<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-05-13|DMY}} |title=Spięcie między Rafałem Trzaskowskim i Karolem Nawrockim. "Decyzjo prezesa" [WIDEO] |url=https://wiadomosci.onet.pl/wybory/wybory-prezydenckie/decyzja-prezesa-tak-rafal-trzaskowski-nazwal-karola-nawrockiego/tseev4x |access-date=2025-07-13}}</ref>

==== Mentzen's campaign ====
Sławomir Mentzen presented himself as the anti-establishment candidate who would take on the "duopoly" of the [[Law and Justice]] and [[Civic Platform]] parties, which have dominated politics since the [[2005 Polish parliamentary election|2005 parliamentary election]].<ref name=Dowell>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-05-08|DMY}} |last=Dowell |first=Stuart |title=Security and conservatism shape Poland's presidential election |url=https://tvpworld.com/86599529/security-and-conservatism-shape-polands-presidential-election |access-date=2025-07-15}}</ref> He was the dominant candidate in social media and among the youth. He also campaigned on polling indicating himself to have the highest chance out of all the right-wing candidates to defeat Trzaskowski in the second round of the election.<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-03-27|DMY}} |last=Bogdańska |first=Katarzyna |title=Mentzen o drugiej turze wyborów. "Mam większe szanse"  |url=https://wiadomosci.wp.pl/mentzen-o-drugiej-turze-wyborow-mam-wieksze-szanse-7139568583535456a |access-date=2025-07-23}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-04-15|DMY}} |last=Rogalski |first=Michał |title=Mentzen powtórzył to zdanie w debacie 12 razy. Sprawdzamy, czy ma rację |url=https://wiadomosci.onet.pl/wybory/wybory-prezydenckie/mentzen-podczas-debaty-powtarzal-jedna-rzecz-sprawdzamy-czy-mial-racje/xt12hm8 |access-date=2025-07-23}}</ref> He focused his campaign on economic and security issues, most prominently tax reform, immigration and military readiness for war.<ref name=mentzenprogram>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-05-15|DMY}} |title=Takie są priorytety Mentzena. Program wyborczy |url=https://www.pap.pl/aktualnosci/program-mentzena-nie-dla-aborcji-konkurencja-w-systemie-ochrony-zdrowia-i-reforma |access-date=2025-07-13}}</ref>

==== Braun's campaign ====
Grzegorz Braun ran on the slogan "This is Poland!". Braun's campaign was also unique in making populist demands, such as the exhumation of the [[Jedwabne pogrom]] victims, releasing classified files on the dissolution of the [[Military Information Services (Poland)|Military Information Services]], and restarting investigations into deaths of [[Jerzy Popiełuszko]], [[Andrzej Lepper]], [[Sławomir Petelicki]] and [[Marek Papała]]. Braun became popular for controversial stunts during his campaign; he organized protests that successfully forced the German supermarket chain [[Lidl]] to resign from building a store near the place of Marian apparitions in [[Gietrzwałd]], winning over voters concerned with preserving Catholic tradition, [[economic nationalism]] and limiting foreign capital in Poland.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.newsweek.pl/opinie/grzegorz-braun-na-wojnie-z-lidlem-wygral-z-pomoca-matki-boskiej-opinia/5n58zl8 |title=Niemcy zostali pokonani, a do zwycięstwa poprowadzili Polaków Matka Boska i Grzegorz Braun |date=29 June 2025 |language=pl |website=[[Newsweek]] |first=Krzysztof |last=Varga}}</ref> Braun's campaign and rhetoric was described by critics as "hostile to democracy, full of conspiracy theories, religiously fundamentalist, and often openly anti-Semitic and anti-Ukrainian",<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.newsweek.pl/polska/polityka/ekscesy-grzegorza-brauna-to-powazne-zagrozenie-panstwo-jest-dzis-bezradne/n0rv7bn |language=pl |website=[[Newsweek]] |title=To nie jest sympatyczna egzotyka. Braun pcha nas w groźnym kierunku |date=17 April 2025 |first=Jakub |last=Majmurek}}</ref> while supporters praised his "fight for truth, authenticity", "soldier-like" dedication to the values of [[God, Honour, Fatherland]], and challenging the submissive attitude of the Polish governments towards Ukraine, Israel and NATO.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.newsweek.pl/polska/polityka/na-kogo-zaglosuja-wyborcy-grzegorza-brauna-warszawa-sie-nimi-nie-interesuje/tb3mrhy |title="Pięknie się wypowiada i porządek chce w kraju zrobić". Na kogo zagłosują wyborcy Brauna |date=26 May 2025 |website=[[Newsweek]] |language=pl |first=Dominik |last=Szczepański}}</ref> His campaign was centered on [[Polish nationalism]], Catholic tradition and opposition to NATO and the European Union.<ref name=Braunwcn>{{cite web |url=https://wszystkoconajwazniejsze.pl/pepites/grzegorz-braun-program-na-wybory-2025/ |language=pl |title=Grzegorz Braun program na wybory 2025 |year=2025 |website=Wszystko Co Najważniejsze}}</ref><ref name=inniprogram>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-05-15|DMY}} |title=Kandydaci spoza czołowej szóstki. Oto najważniejsze punkty ich programów wyborczych |url=https://www.pap.pl/aktualnosci/kandydaci-spoza-czolowej-szostki-oto-najwazniejsze-punkty-ich-programow-wyborczych |access-date=2025-07-13}}</ref>

==== Other campaigns ==== 
Szymon Hołownia promised to support "[[local communities|local Poland]]", [[decentralization|decentralize]] the state administration and apply [[referendum]]s to resolve polarizing issues. He presented himself as a "candidate for the people", as opposed to a partisan candidate. Hołownia highlighted [[energy transition]], housing prices, national security and children's safety from technology addiction as campaign issues.<ref name=holowniaprogram>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-05-15|DMY}} |title=Rozwój Polski lokalnej, brak smartfonów w szkołach, "tak" dla związków partnerskich. Poznaj program Szymon Hołowni |url=https://www.pap.pl/aktualnosci/rozwoj-polski-lokalnej-brak-smartfonow-w-szkolach-tak-dla-zwiazkow-partnerskich-poznaj |access-date=2025-07-13}}</ref>

Adrian Zandberg, a leftwing candidate, contrasted himself against former party ally Magdalena Biejat in his criticism of the ruling coalition, which he criticized as corrupt and ineffectual in resolving problems of the citizens.<ref name=debataZB>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-05-12|DMY}} |title=Debata prezydencka. Adrian Zandberg uderzył w Magdalenę Biejat. "O czym ty mówisz?" |url=https://wiadomosci.onet.pl/wybory/wybory-prezydenckie/adrian-zandberg-ostro-skrytykowal-magdalene-biejat-o-czym-ty-mowisz/y3qz3b5 |access-date=2025-07-23}}</ref> He presented himself as an anti-establishment candidate, fighting for votes among Mentzen's young anti-establishment base.<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-05-16|DMY}} |last=Baranowska |first=Kamila |title=Od Mentzena do Zandberga i z powrotem. Zaskakujące przepływy wyborców |url=https://wydarzenia.interia.pl/wybory/prezydenckie/news-od-mentzena-do-zandberga-i-z-powrotem-zaskakujace-przeplywy,nId,21808881 |access-date=2025-07-23}}</ref> Zandberg's campaign oriented around infrastructural development, reducing housing prices and improving Poland's healthcare system.<ref name=zandbergprogram>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-05-15|DMY}} |title=Tak wygląda program Zandberga: atomowa Polska i 8 proc. PKB na zdrowie |url=https://www.pap.pl/aktualnosci/tak-wyglada-program-zandberga-atomowa-polska-i-8-proc-pkb-na-zdrowie |access-date=2025-07-13}}</ref>

Magdalena Biejat, a former member of Zandberg's [[Razem]] party, criticized Zandberg for his opposition to the ruling government, highlighting the pro-government [[The Left (Poland)|Left]]'s accomplishments as allies of the Prime Minister.<ref name=debataZB/> Biejat focused on issues such as housing prices, legalization of abortion and secularization.<ref name=biejatprogram>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-05-15|DMY}} |title=Legalna aborcja, tanie mieszkania. Program wyborczy Magdaleny Biejat |url=https://www.pap.pl/aktualnosci/program-biejat-walka-z-kryzysem-mieszkaniowym-aborcja-do-12-tygodnia-ciazy-i-swieckie |access-date=2025-07-13}}</ref>

=== Economy ===
Nawrocki's program was described as [[economic interventionism|economically interventionist]],<ref>{{cite web |date={{date|2025-06-02|DMY}} |title=Karol Nawrocki's Presidential Agenda: Catholic values and national sovereignty |url=https://ieu-monitoring.com/editorial/karol-nawrockis-presidential-agenda-catholic-values-and-national-sovereignty/828303?utm_source=ieu-portal |website=Insight EU Monitoring |quote="President-elect Karol Nawrocki’s campaign programme outlines a conservative and economically interventionist vision for Poland." |archive-date=9 June 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250609122646/https://ieu-monitoring.com/editorial/karol-nawrockis-presidential-agenda-catholic-values-and-national-sovereignty/828303?utm_source=ieu-portal |url-status=live}}</ref> or economically left-wing.<ref>{{bulleted list|{{cite web |url=https://www.pollbludger.net/2025/06/04/south-korea-and-poland-elections-wrap/ |title=South Korea and Poland elections wrap |date=4 June 2025 |first=Adrian |last=Beaumont |quote="At Sunday's Polish presidential runoff election, Karol Nawrocki, the candidate of the economically left but socially conservative Law and Justice (PiS) defeated Rafał Trzaskowski." |website=Poll Bludger |archive-date=5 June 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250605031442/https://www.pollbludger.net/2025/06/04/south-korea-and-poland-elections-wrap/ |url-status=live}}|{{cite web |website=[[BBC News]] |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cgegn1ggxn8o |title=Warsaw's liberal mayor narrowly wins Polish presidential vote |location=Warsaw |first=Adam |last=Easton |date=19 May 2025 |quote="Many would support Nawrocki for his Catholic, family-oriented views, but they dislike PiS's left-wing economic policy of generous state benefits."}}}}</ref> Nawrocki described himself as a strong supporter of armaments and social investment programmes. Nawrocki supported large economic investments; he strongly supports the [[Central Communication Port]] ({{langx|pl|Centralny Port Komunikacyjny}}, CPK) project,<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-05-23|DMY}} |title=Nawrocki popiera postulaty ws. CPK. "Zapraszam na spotkanie" |url=https://dorzeczy.pl/ekonomia/730638/karol-nawrocki-popiera-postulaty-tak-dla-cpk.html |access-date=2025-07-12}}</ref> and praised the [[Central Industrial Region (Poland)|Central Industrial Region]] and [[Stocznia Gdynia]] schemes developed in the interwar [[Second Polish Republic]].<ref name="onet_eko">{{cite web |date={{date|2024-11-24|DMY}} |last=Dybińska |first=Katarzyna |title=Karol Nawrocki o gospodarce. "Jest gorzej". Obiecuje zwolnienie z podatku |url=https://biznes.interia.pl/gospodarka/news-karol-nawrocki-o-gospodarce-jest-gorzej-obiecuje-zwolnienie-,nId,7862539 |website=interia.pl |language=pl |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241124174814/https://biznes.interia.pl/gospodarka/news-karol-nawrocki-o-gospodarce-jest-gorzej-obiecuje-zwolnienie-,nId,7862539 |archive-date=24 November 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> Nawrocki expressed his fascination with other large investments such as the [[Vistula Spit canal]] and [[Świnoujście LNG terminal]], wanting to pursue similar undertakings.<ref>{{cite web |date={{date|2024-11-09|DMY}} |last=Nawrocki |first=Karol |title=The Polish Anchor of Freedom |url=https://eng.ipn.gov.pl/en/news/11613,ARTICLE-by-Karol-Nawrocki-PhD-quotThe-Polish-Anchor-of-Freedomquot.html |website=[[Institute of National Remembrance]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241126210829/https://eng.ipn.gov.pl/en/news/11613,ARTICLE-by-Karol-Nawrocki-PhD-quotThe-Polish-Anchor-of-Freedomquot.html |archive-date=26 November 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> He promised investments of new infrastructure in every [[gmina]].<ref name=nawrockiprogram/>

During the campaign, Trzaskowski was described as [[neoliberal]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Polonia, liberalismo y extrema derecha |url=https://www.jornada.com.mx/noticia/2025/09/06/opinion/polonia-liberalismo-y-extrema-derecha |language=es |date=6 September 2025 |first=Maciek |last=Wiśniewski |website=[[La Jornada]]}}</ref> He opposed increasing social spending and expressed openess to [[austerity]] policies.<ref name="verfassung"/> He proposed to remove child benefits from unemployed Ukrainian refugees,<ref>{{cite web |url=https://transform-network.net/blog/analysis/end-of-the-pis-ko-era-brief-reflections-on-polands-election/ |title=End of the PiS–KO Era? Brief Reflections on Poland's Election |date=21 May 2025 |first=Gavin |last=Rae |website=Transform Network}}</ref> endorsed Rafał Brzoska's "deregulation task force" and wanted to accelerate the process of deregulation,<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.polskieradio.pl/395/11354/artykul/3528795,centrist-trzaskowski-declines-to-sign%C2%A0farright%C2%A0pledge%C2%A0ahead-of-polish-presidential-runoff |title=Centrist Trzaskowski declines to sign far-right pledge ahead of Polish presidential runoff |date=26 May 2025 |website=[[Polskie Radio]] |quote="Asked whether he supported deregulation, Trzaskowski replied that he would like the work of a deregulation task force, established by the government and led by entrepreneur Rafał Brzoska, to accelerate."}}</ref> and pledged to sign the government's bill to cut health insurance tax for entrepreneurs.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.gazetaprawna.pl/wiadomosci/kraj/artykuly/9792336,trzaskowski-jako-prezydent-podpisalbym-ustawe-obnizajaca-skladke-zdro.html |title=Trzaskowski: Jako prezydent podpisałbym ustawę obniżającą składkę zdrowotną |date=7 May 2025 |website=[[Dziennik Gazeta Prawna]] |language=pl |first=Urszula |last=Wróblewska}}</ref>

Braun promised to oppose any budget bill "that allocates a single [[złoty]] to matters unrelated to Poles"; this included opposing welfare benefits for Ukrainian immigrants and Jewish property claims. He also demanded a reversal of "selling off Polish land and resources". He argued that Poland should generate energy from both renewable and non-renewable sources, focusing on lowering life costs instead of minimizing the environmental impact.<ref name=Braunonet>{{cite web |url=https://wiadomosci.onet.pl/wybory/wybory-prezydenckie/wybory-prezydenckie-2025-grzegorz-braun-program-wyborczy/r55k6f0 |title=Wybory prezydenckie 2025. Grzegorz Braun – program wyborczy |date=16 May 2025 |website=[[onet.pl]] |language=pl}}</ref>

