=== Welfare and taxation ===
Nawrocki supported social welfare programmes,<ref name=Materna/> calling for "a welfare state with zero VAT on food".<ref>{{cite web |date={{date|2025-04-17|DMY}} |last=Żuraw |first=Magdalena |title=Without Foreign Ideologies, Safe and Normal... This Is Nawrocki's Vision for Poland |url=https://polanddaily24.com/without-foreign-ideologies-safe-and-normal-this-is-nawrockis-vision-for-poland/poland-today/54332 |website=Poland Daily 24 |archive-date=17 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250417071303/https://polanddaily24.com/without-foreign-ideologies-safe-and-normal-this-is-nawrockis-vision-for-poland/poland-today/54332 |url-status=live}}</ref> He stressed the lack of transport in Poland and has pledged to develop rail infrastructure in underdeveloped regions of the country.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.rp.pl/polityka/art41493771-karol-nawrocki-rozpoczal-kampanie-powiedzial-ze-polacy-kochaja-kolej |title=Karol Nawrocki rozpoczął kampanię. Powiedział, że Polacy kochają kolej |date=25 November 2024 |website=[[Rzeczpospolita (newspaper)|Rzeczpospolita]] |language=pl |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241125195857/https://www.rp.pl/polityka/art41493771-karol-nawrocki-rozpoczal-kampanie-powiedzial-ze-polacy-kochaja-kolej |archive-date=25 November 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> His other proposals include abolishing tax on savings and increasing the annual indexation of pensions.<ref name="Bloomberg">{{cite web |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2025-03-02/polish-opposition-candidate-floats-tax-cuts-in-presidential-race |title=Polish Opposition Candidate Floats Tax Cuts in Presidential Race |date=2 March 2025 |first=Konrad |last=Krasuski |website=[[Bloomberg News]] |archive-date=6 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250406015320/https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2025-03-02/polish-opposition-candidate-floats-tax-cuts-in-presidential-race |url-status=live}}</ref> He also expressed [[welfare chauvinism|welfare chauvinist]] views — believing that Poles are "treated worse in their own country than immigrants", Nawrocki argued that social benefits in Poland should be for Poles only, and pensions for unemployed Ukrainian refugees should be eliminated; additionally, Polish citizens should have a priority in healthcare, school and kindergarten queues.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://polanddaily24.com/this-will-be-the-most-significant-legal-change-in-recent-years-nawrocki-makes-a-promise/poland-today/53948 |title="This will be the most significant legal change in recent years." Nawrocki makes a promise |date=8 April 2025 |website=Poland Daily 24 |archive-date=8 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250408193802/https://polanddaily24.com/this-will-be-the-most-significant-legal-change-in-recent-years-nawrocki-makes-a-promise/poland-today/53948 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://notesfrompoland.com/2025/04/09/presidential-candidate-pledges-law-to-ensure-poles-cant-be-treated-worse-than-immigrants/ |title=Presidential candidate pledges law to ensure "Poles can't be treated worse than immigrants" |date=9 April 2025 |first=Daniel |last=Tilles |archive-date=9 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250409141357/https://notesfrompoland.com/2025/04/09/presidential-candidate-pledges-law-to-ensure-poles-cant-be-treated-worse-than-immigrants/ |url-status=live}}</ref>

Mentzen's campaign oriented around the lowering of taxes, removing the [[inheritance tax]], [[capital gains tax]], and simplifying the [[personal income tax]], [[corporate tax]], [[value-added tax]], among others.<ref name=mentzenprogram/>

Braun supported the abolition of [[income tax]], [[corporation tax]] and compulsory health insurance.<ref name=Braunonet/>

