In the first round Trzaskowski came first with 31% of the vote, with Nawrocki coming in second with 30%, advancing to the second round. The right-wing candidates Nawrocki, Mentzen and Braun overperformed polls, received 30%, 15% and 6% respectively, finishing second, third and fourth.<ref name="WL">{{cite web |last1=Easton |first1=Adam |title=Warsaw's liberal mayor leads Polish presidential vote – exit poll |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cgegn1ggxn8o |website=[[BBC]] |access-date=18 May 2025}}</ref><ref name="SW">{{cite news |date=2025-05-19 |title=Prof. Leszczyński: Wynik Grzegorza Brauna w I turze wyborów prezydenckich "szokująco wysoki" |url=https://www.bankier.pl/wiadomosc/Prof-Leszczynski-Wynik-Grzegorza-Brauna-w-I-turze-wyborow-prezydenckich-szokujaco-wysoki-8944932.html |access-date=2025-05-20}}</ref> Hołownia and Biejat underperformed, coming fifth and seventh, the latter coming below her left-wing rival, Zandberg.<ref name="IZ">{{cite web |date=2025-05-19 |title=Hołownia największym przegranym? W sondażu za Braunem i Zandbergiem |url=https://businessinsider.com.pl/wiadomosci/wyniki-wyborow-2025-holownia-daleko-poza-podium-najwiekszy-przegrany-wyborow/pmc60h4 |access-date=2025-05-20}}</ref><ref name="PB">{{cite web |date=2025-05-19 |title=Antyrządowy Zandberg górą w rywalizacji z prorządową Biejat |url=https://wyborcza.pl/7,75968,31950601,antyrzadowy-zandberg-gora-w-rywalizacji-z-prorzadowa-biejat.html |access-date=2025-05-20}}</ref>

In the second round, according to an exit poll by [[Ipsos]], Trzaskowski received 50.3% of the vote and Nawrocki 49.7%, however, the margin of 0.6% was within the margin of error. Shortly after the poll was released, Trzaskowski claimed victory giving a speech to supporters in Warsaw.<ref>{{cite web |last1=GERA |first1=VANESSA |title=An exit poll in Poland's presidential runoff shows the race is too close to call |url=https://apnews.com/article/poland-presidential-election-e9ae2771d1c774528bff6c6bc9e90e26 |access-date=1 June 2025 |website=[[Associated Press]]|date=June 2025 }}</ref> A late poll, released by Ipsos at 23:00, later indicated that Nawrocki came first with 50.7% of the vote.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Strzelecki |first1=Marek |last2=Koper |first2=Anna |title=Poland's Nawrocki on course for tight presidential election win |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/europe/pro-eu-maga-visions-clash-polands-closely-fought-presidential-runoff-2025-06-01/ |website=[[Reuters]] |access-date=1 June 2025}}</ref> After all votes were counted, Nawrocki's vote share ended with 10,606,877 votes (50.89%), against Trzaskowski's 10,237,286 (49.11%).<ref name=BBC/>

