== Conduct ==
=== PiS campaign funding dispute ===
In the lead-up to the election, a portion of the [[party subsidy]] was withheld from [[Law and Justice]]. The [[Law and Justice#2024 party subsidy issue|issue]] emerged after the [[National Electoral Commission (Poland)|National Electoral Commission]] ruled the party's financial report for the 2023 parliamentary campaign, and consequently its 2023 annual report, to be flawed. As a result, both the campaign dotation and the annual subsidy were reduced by approximately 11{{nbsp}}million{{nbsp}}[[Polish złoty|PLN]]. The ruling was appealed to the [[Supreme Court of Poland]], where the Extraordinary Review and Public Affairs Chamber decided in favour of the party. This legally bound the commission to change its verdict, which happened on {{date|2024-12-30|DMY}}. However, as the legitimacy of this particular Supreme Court chamber has been questioned by the ruling government and the [[Court of Justice of the European Union]] due to the ongoing [[Polish constitutional crisis|rule of law crisis since 2017]], the Minister of Finance [[Andrzej Domański]] refused to transfer the disputed funds.<ref>{{cite web |date={{date|2025-01-07|DMY}} |last2=Kostecki |last1=Litwin |first2=Marcin |first1=Piotr  |title=Zablokowana subwencja dla PiS. Wyjaśniamy spór wokół decyzji PKW |url=https://demagog.org.pl/analizy_i_raporty/zablokowana-subwencja-dla-pis-wyjasniamy-spor-wokol-decyzji-pkw/ |website=Demagog |access-date={{date|2025-04-27|DMY}} |language=pl}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-01-03|DMY}} |title=PiS nie otrzyma subwencji? Czarnek: Pozwanie ministra finansów może być koniecznością |url=http://bankier.pl/wiadomosc/PiS-nie-otrzyma-subwencji-Czarnek-Pozwanie-ministra-finansow-moze-byc-koniecznoscia-8869177.html |access-date={{date|2025-04-27|DMY}} |work=Bankier.pl |language=pl}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-03-10|DMY}} |title=Domański: nie dam się zastraszyć PiS-owi, czekam na wykładnię PKW |url=https://www.pap.pl/aktualnosci/domanski-nie-dam-sie-zastraszyc-pis-owi-czekam-na-wykladnie-pkw |access-date={{date|2025-04-27|DMY}} |work=pap.pl |publisher=[[Polish Press Agency]] |language=pl}}</ref> Ultimately, Nawrocki had to conduct his campaign without the funds transferred to PiS.<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-05-18|DMY}} |last=Nowakowska |first=Karolina |title=Wybory prezydenckie 2025. Nawrocki: Były to wybory nieuczciwe |url=https://www.gazetaprawna.pl/wiadomosci/kraj/artykuly/9801342,wybory-prezydenckie-2025-nawrocki-byly-to-wybory-nieuczciwe.html |access-date={{date|2025-05-21|DMY}}}}</ref> Therefore, he had to finance his campaign through a [[grassroot]] effort – around 50,000 supporters donated to his election effort.<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-06-02|DMY}} |last=Borzozowski |first=Adam |title=Szef sztabu Karola Nawrockiego: Badania mówiły, że nasz kandydat nie wejdzie do II tury! |url=https://www.se.pl/wybory/prezydenckie/szef-sztabu-karola-nawrockiego-badania-mowily-ze-nasz-kandydat-nie-wejdzie-do-ii-tury-aa-mxrv-R7K6-zetB.html |access-date=2025-06-03}}</ref>

=== Electoral Protection Movement ===
PiS launched the "Electoral Protection Movement" ({{langx|pl|Ruch Ochrony Wyborów}}), operated primarily by former minister [[Przemysław Czarnek]],<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2024-12-21|DMY}} |title=PiS tworzy ruch ochrony wyborów. Kluczową rolę mają dla Czarnka |url=https://wiadomosci.wp.pl/pis-tworzy-ruch-ochrony-wyborow-kluczowa-role-maja-dla-czarnka-7105625898232544a |access-date={{date|2025-02-27|DMY}}}}</ref> with the intention of safeguarding the democratic conduct of the election and protecting it from [[electoral fraud]].<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-02-25|DMY}} |title=Czarnek ogłasza ochronę wyborów, jakiej nie było. "W uczciwych wyborach wygra Nawrocki" |url=https://wyborcza.pl/7,75398,31721219,czarnek-oglasza-ochrone-wyborow-jakiej-nie-bylo-w-uczciwych.html |archive-url=https://archive.today/20250226081142/https://wyborcza.pl/7,75398,31721219,czarnek-oglasza-ochrone-wyborow-jakiej-nie-bylo-w-uczciwych.html |archive-date={{date|2025-02-26|DMY}} |access-date={{date|2025-02-27|DMY}}}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-02-24|DMY}} |title=PiS będzie pilnować wyborów. Czarnek: Podwijamy rękawy |url=https://dorzeczy.pl/kraj/694531/ruch-ochrony-wyborow-pis-bedzie-pilnowac-wyborow.html |access-date={{date|2025-02-27|DMY}}}}</ref>

=== Illegal funding for Trzaskowski and OSCE report ===
[[Wirtualna Polska]] detailed allegations of an illegal advertising campaign on [[Facebook]] which favored Trzaskowski while attacking Nawrocki and Mentzen, with the advertising campaign having ties to the foreign company Estratos Digital GmbH based in Vienna and headed by two Hungarians {{mdash}} [[Ádám Ficsor]] and [[Viktor Szigetvári]], with capital tied to the American [[Democratic Party (United States)|Democratic Party]].<ref>{{Cite web |date={{date|2025-05-15|DMY}} |title=Ujawniamy. Ingerencja w wybory, spoty bez autora i Akcja Demokracja |url=https://wiadomosci.wp.pl/ujawniamy-ingerencja-w-wybory-spoty-bez-autora-i-akcja-demokracja-7156892271278624a |access-date=2025-05-22 |website=WP Wiadomości |language=pl}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-05-16|DMY}} |title=Trzaskowski odpowie za nielegalną kampanię? Jest głos z PKW. "To może być oczywiście podstawą odrzucenia sprawozdania finansowego" |url=https://wpolityce.pl/polityka/729604-trzaskowski-odpowie-za-nielegalna-kampanie-jest-glos-z-pkw |access-date=2025-06-22}}</ref> The [[Organization for Security and Co-operation in Europe]] (OSCE) and [[Parliamentary Assembly of the Council of Europe]] (PACE) investigated the election and confirmed the allegations.<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-06-03|DMY}} |last=Słowik |first=Patryk |title=Obserwatorzy OBWE i Rady Europy krytycznie o NASK i reklamach promujących Rafała Trzaskowskiego |url=https://wiadomosci.wp.pl/obserwatorzy-obwe-i-rady-europy-krytycznie-o-nask-i-reklamach-promujacych-rafala-trzaskowskiego-7163699091700480a |access-date=2025-06-05}}</ref>

The OSCE-PACE report further pointed out the bias of government institutions like [[Naukowa i Akademicka Sieć Komputerowa|NASK]] in favor of Trzaskowski. According to the report, public media, like [[Telewizja Polska|TVP]], was also biased, and depicted Nawrocki in a negative light.<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-06-04|DMY}} |last=Mularczyk |first=Krzysztof |title=Polish Government's candidate had 'unfair advantage', says OSCE election report |url=https://brusselssignal.eu/2025/06/polish-governments-candidate-had-unfair-advantage-says-osce-election-report/ |access-date=2025-06-05}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-06-02|DMY}} |last=Wesołowski |first=Timur |title=Raport OBWE ws. drugiej tury wyborów. "Głębia polaryzacji politycznej" |url=https://wiadomosci.gazeta.pl/wiadomosci/7,114884,31992667,raport-obwe-ws-drugiej-tury-wyborow-glebia-polaryzacji-politycznej.html |access-date=2025-06-05}}</ref> The Polish [[National Broadcasting Council]] released a report accusing TVP and TVN of supporting the Trzaskowski campaign, and TV Republika of supporting Nawrocki.<ref>{{cite news |title=KRRiT: TVP i TVN pokazują pozytywnie Trzaskowskiego, Republika Nawrockiego |url=https://www.wirtualnemedia.pl/artykul/krrit-monitoring-wybory-prezydenckie-tvp-tvn-polsat-republika-rafal-trzaskowski-karol-nawrocki-slawomir-mentzen |access-date=2025-04-16}}</ref>

Shortly before the first round of the election, [[SMS]] spam messages were reported encouraging voters to vote for Trzaskowski. Trzaskowski's campaign staff distanced themselves from the messages and informed that they were notifying law enforcement of the incident.<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-05-15|DMY}} |last=Wesołowski |first=Timur |title=Polacy dostają dziwne SMS-y o Rafale Trzaskowskim. Trwa zmasowany atak, sztab reaguje |url=https://wiadomosci.gazeta.pl/wiadomosci/7,114884,31937486,polacy-dostaja-sms-y-dot-rafala-trzaskowskiego-trwa-zmasowany.html |access-date=2025-07-13}}</ref>

=== Social media ===
The election marked a shift in which social media assumed a significantly greater role, increasingly rivaling traditional media for public attention.<ref name=socialmedia>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-01-02|DMY}} |last=Tomasik |first=Michał |title=Bez kontroli i bez reguł. Kampania w internecie już szaleje: prosto, krótko i nie na temat |url=https://www.polityka.pl/tygodnikpolityka/kraj/2283561,1,bez-kontroli-i-bez-regul-kampania-w-internecie-juz-szaleje-prosto-krotko-i-nie-na-temat.read |access-date=2025-07-09}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-05-30|DMY}} |last=Kolanko |first=Michał |title=Michał Kolanko: Kampania wyborcza 2025 przyniosła medialną rewolucję |url=https://www.rp.pl/publicystyka/art42413461-michal-kolanko-kampania-wyborcza-2025-przyniosla-medialna-rewolucje |work=[[Rzeczpospolita (newspaper)|Rzeczpospolita]] |access-date=2025-11-14}}</ref> The campaign also marked a realignment in the social media landscape, as right-wing ascendancy replaced what had traditionally been a liberal-dominated sphere.<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-10-10|DMY}} |last=Pilawa |first=Konstanty |title=Koniec hegemonii liberałów w internecie |url=https://www.rp.pl/plus-minus/art43154481-koniec-hegemonii-liberalow-w-internecie |work=[[Rzeczpospolita (newspaper)|Rzeczpospolita]] |access-date=2025-10-11}}</ref> In the first round, Sławomir Mentzen dominated the internet sphere, getting 15x as much internet traffic as Nawrocki and 10x as much as Trzaskowski in January.<ref name=socialmedia/> Between January and April, Mentzen received 24 million interactions (likes, comments, shares) with his social media posts, Nawrocki received 6 million, and Trzaskowski 5 million.<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-04-18|DMY}} |title=Jeden kandydat zdominował internet. "Tiktokizacja polityki" |url=https://www.pap.pl/aktualnosci/jeden-kandydat-zdominowal-internet-tiktokizacja-polityki-raport-dla-pap |access-date=2025-07-13}}</ref> Negative campaigning on social media occupied a plurality — 1/3rds of election-related activity,<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-06-15|DMY}} |title=Podsumowanie kampanii prezydenckiej w internecie. Jakie tematy najczęściej poruszali kandydaci? |url=https://www.pap.pl/aktualnosci/jakie-tematy-najczesciej-poruszali-kandydaci-podsumowanie-kampanii-prezydenckiej-w |access-date=2025-07-09}}</ref> with the tag "#AnyoneButTrzaskowski" ({{langx|pl|ByleNieTrzaskowski}}) trending on social media as part of Nawrocki's second round campaign.<ref name=newsweekkulisy/>

=== Election complaints ===
By the end of the deadline for filing them, the [[Supreme Court of Poland]] received 54,645 election complaints,<ref name=giertychowki>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-07-01|DMY}} |title=Sąd Najwyższy orzeka w sprawie ważności wyborów prezydenckich. Adam Bodnar wyłączony? |url=https://www.rp.pl/prawo-dla-ciebie/art42635271-sad-najwyzszy-orzeka-w-sprawie-waznosci-wyborow-prezydenckich-adam-bodnar-wylaczony |access-date=2025-07-01}}</ref> significantly more than the 5,800 complaints following the [[2020 Polish presidential election|2020 presidential election]],<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2020-08-02|DMY}} |title=SN rozpatrzył wszystkie protesty wyborcze. 92 uznał za zasadne  |url=https://wiadomosci.onet.pl/kraj/wybory-prezydenckie-2020-sn-rozpatrzyl-prawie-wszystkie-protesty-wyborcze/rh6wbhw |access-date=2025-06-23}}</ref> but significantly less than the 600,000 complaints following the [[1995 Polish presidential election|1995 presidential election]].<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2010-07-02|DMY}} |title=Protesty wyborcze - w 1995 r. zgłoszono ich 600 tys. |url=https://wydarzenia.interia.pl/kraj/news-protesty-wyborcze-w-1995-r-zgloszono-ich-600-tys,nId,883139 |access-date=2025-06-22}}</ref> According to the [[Supreme Court of Poland|Supreme Court]], the overwhelming majority were copies of a complaint template shared by [[election denial]]ist [[Roman Giertych]], colloquially titled "giertychówki".<ref name=giertychowki/> The complaints concerned largely the incidents of the results being swapped in a few polling stations, after it was found that Nawrocki performed abnormally well in some isolated stations that heavily favored Trzaskowski in the first round.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://wiadomosci.onet.pl/wybory/wybory-prezydenckie/sedzia-sn-o-bledach-w-komisjach-wyborczych-nie-pamietam-takiej-sytuacji/tbw256r |title=Sędzia SN o błędach w komisjach wyborczych. "Nie pamiętam takiej sytuacji" |first=Magdalena |last=Gałczyńska |date=21 June 2025 |language=pl |website=[[Onet.pl]]}}</ref> The campaign of Trzaskowski also filed a complaint and created a website for its supporters to help them file one as well. The Supreme Court ruled to recount the votes in 13 such stations.<ref name="dorzeczy_rig"/>

Anomalies were found in some voting station protocols where both candidates lost votes relative to the first round. Journalists investigating the situation have asserted that in 15 polling stations the results may have been flipped, but this would not impact the result of the election as the number of votes potentially affected was well below the margin of victory for Nawrocki.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bojakowski |first=Jakub |date=2025-06-05 |title=Znikające głosy i inne "cudy nad urną". Rzecznik PKW zabrał głos |url=https://www.wprost.pl/kraj/12036835/bledy-w-liczeniu-glosow-w-ii-turze-rzecznik-pkw-skomentowal-watpliwosci.html |access-date=2025-06-05 |website=Wprost |language=pl}}</ref> On 12 June, the [[Supreme Court of Poland]] ordered a recount in 13 commissions, 0.04% of all 32,143 commissions.<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-06-12|DMY}} |title=Protesty wyborcze. SN zdecydował ws. ponownego przeliczenia głosów |url=https://dorzeczy.pl/kraj/740748/wybory-prezydenckie-sn-dopuszcza-ponowne-przeliczenie-glosow.html |access-date=2025-06-12}}</ref> On 1 July 2025, the Supreme Court certified Nawrocki's victory as president.<ref>{{cite news |date=1 July 2025 |title=Polish supreme court ratifies nationalist's presidential vote win |url=https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20250701-polish-supreme-court-ratifies-nationalist-s-presidential-vote-win |access-date=2 July 2025}}</ref>

On 18 June, the Polish [[Minister of Justice (Poland)|Minister of Justice]] and [[Public Prosecutor General (Poland)|Public Prosecutor General]] [[Adam Bodnar]] announced that the [[National Public Prosecutor's Office]] would review the ballots in 250 selected voting stations where "serious anomalies" were considered likely.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://wiadomosci.onet.pl/kraj/adam-bodnar-o-ponownym-przeliczeniu-glosow-zakonczy-sie-w-przyszlym-tygodniu/5fb12lw |language=pl |title=Ponowne przeliczanie głosów w komisjach. Adam Bodnar podaje ważny termin |date=18 July 2025 |website=[[onet.pl]]}}</ref> On 25 July, Prosecutor's Office announced the results of the investigation — out of the 250 voting stations reviewed, irregularities were found in 84 (33%). In 42 of those, the irregularities were at the expense of Trzaskowski, in 34 they were at the expense of Nawrocki, and in 8 the irregularities only concerned invalid votes. The investigation concluded that compared to the official results in the suspected voting stations, Nawrocki received 1538 less votes, and Trzaskowski 1541 more. Therefore, it did not affect the election's results.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://tvn24.pl/polska/wybory-prezydenckie-nieprawidlowosci-przy-liczeniu-glosow-prokuratura-krajowa-przedstawila-raport-st8572320 |language=pl |title=Nieprawidłowości przy liczeniu głosów. Jest raport |date=25 July 2025 |website=[[TVN24]]}}</ref> Later, on 6 August, the Prosecutor's Office declared that it had made a mistake, and that the discrepancy in votes was even smaller than reported — Nawrocki received 1239 less votes and Trzaskowski 1241 more.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://wiadomosci.wp.pl/bledy-podczas-liczenia-glosow-aktualizacja-komunikatu-prokuratury-7186680309676800a |language=pl |title=Błędy podczas liczenia głosów. Aktualizacja komunikatu prokuratury |first=Aleksandra |last=Wieczorek |date=7 August 2025 |website=[[wp.pl]]}}</ref> It also stated that the official election results remain unchanged because the investigation was only meant to determine whether a crime had taken place or not, and "was not intended to determine the results of the presidential election".<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.gazetaprawna.pl/wiadomosci/kraj/artykuly/9849218,blad-na-1500-glosow-prokuratura-ujawnia-nieprawidlowosci-w-wyborach-p.html |title=Błąd na 1500 głosów. Prokuratura ujawnia nieprawidłowości w wyborach prezydenckich |date=25 July 2025 |website=[[Dziennik Gazeta Prawna|Gazeta Prawna]] |language=pl}}</ref>

== Analysis ==
=== Ruling government ===
Commenting on the assessment of the Tusk's government during the election, political scientist Gavin Rae argued that it showed misalignment with its promises from the [[2023 Polish parliamentary election]], and continuity with the right-wing policies of the previous government led by [[Law and Justice]]:{{blockquote|text=There has been little progress on women’s and LGBT rights. Despite the propaganda about its economic record, many Poles have had to work even harder to maintain their basic living standards, with 40% of people forced to restrict their spending to make ends meet. With Tusk introducing a new round of deregulation, public services – the health service in particular – have continued to deteriorate, leaving many with inadequate care.  
:
At the same time, the KO did much to extend the right-wing policies of the PiS. It has intensified the anti-migrant atmosphere which has long been building in the country, cancelling the right to asylum for some refugees crossing into Poland from Belarus and attempting to push them back across the border. Rather than taking meaningful steps to reverse the PiS legal reforms – designed to consolidate power in the executive – it has pursued a similar course of action to its predecessor: seizing control of the Polish public broadcaster by firing its directors and replacing them with sympathetic ones.<ref name="nlr_gov">{{cite journal |journal=[[New Left Review]] |issn=0028-6060 |title=Weak Myths |first=Gavin |last=Rae |date=6 June 2025 |volume=6 |publisher=Sidecar |doi=10.64590/gay |issue=124 |article-number=706 }}</ref>}}

[[Bright Blue (organisation)|Bright Blue]] wrote that "As it stands, Tusk’s grand coalition, despite Tusk having campaigned on a centre-left platform, is proving surprisingly centre-right". It noted the government's anti-immigration policies such as sharpening border controls, temporarily suspending the right of asylum, reducing the number of visas issued. Additionally, the organization noted Tusk's call for "an enormous deregulatory effort" in order to make Poland and Europe a "more competitive economic environment than the USA".<ref>{{cite journal |url=https://www.brightblue.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Right-road.pdf |title=The right road: The future of the European centre-right |first1=Bartek |last1=Staniszewski |first2=William |last2=Prescott |first3=Joe |last3=Harrison |first4=Ryan |last4=Shorthouse |isbn=978-1-911128-80-9 |date=June 2025 |publisher=Konrad Adenauer Stiftung |journal=[[Bright Blue (organisation)|Bright Blue]] |page=206}}</ref> [[Verfassungsblog]] wrote:{{blockquote|text=The so-called “15 October Coalition” – an alliance of the liberal Civic Platform (PO), the Left, and the conservative Third Way – came to power in late 2023 in the atmosphere of democratic awakening and civic mobilization. Yet, despite its progressive commitments, the government soon shifted to the right. Key demands from its electoral base – including abortion reform and legal recognition of civil partnerships – were quietly sidelined. More tellingly, the coalition maintained several PiS-era policies, particularly its hardline stance on migration at the Belarusian border, effectively mirroring the very approach it had vocally condemned.<ref name="verfassung">{{cite journal |url=https://verfassungsblog.de/poland-presidential-election-2025/ |title=Anatomy of a Liberal Fall: Poland's 2025 Presidential Election |first=Wojciech |last=Zomerski |date=11 June 2025 |doi=10.59704/ee63bc06c3062698 |journal=[[Verfassungsblog]]|doi-access=free |hdl=1814/94924 |hdl-access=free }}</ref>}}

=== Election results ===
The election was similar to the [[2024 United States presidential election]], which was won by [[Republican Party (United States)|Republican]] [[Donald Trump]] by 1.5% over [[Democratic Party (United States)|Democrat]] [[Kamala Harris]].<ref>{{Cite news|title=Trump wins the US Presidency|publisher=AP News|date=2024-11-06|url=https://apnews.com/live/trump-harris-election-updates-11-5-2024|access-date=2024-11-06|archive-date=November 8, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241108182720/https://apnews.com/live/trump-harris-election-updates-11-5-2024|url-status=live}}</ref> The defeats of Harris and Trzaskowski also showed that [[Right-wing populism|right-wing populism]] had staying power, even in countries known for their liberal traditions.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://verfassungsblog.de/populism-poland/|date=December 16, 2025|website=Verfassungsblog|first1=Wojciech|title=Populism Is Here to Stay|last1=Zomerski|access-date=February 25, 2026}}</ref> Trump himself endorsed Nawrocki.

[[Verfassungsblog]] wrote:{{blockquote|text=In any case, the outcome was predictable and mirrored [[Kamala Harris 2024 presidential campaign|Kamala Harris’s 2024 campaign]] mistakes: Trzaskowski failed to win over conservatives while demobilizing much of his progressive base.<ref name="verfassung"/>}} 

Both elections showed an intensely polarized electorate and strong educational polarization.<ref name="Global-Divide">{{Cite web |last1=Higgins |first1=Andrew |date=2 June 2025 |title=Caught Between Two Wests: New Global Divide Runs Straight Through Poland |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/06/02/world/europe/poland-president-election-results.html |access-date=July 23, 2025 |website=The New York Times |quote=The country's government is centrist, with deep ties to Brussels. Its new president is a Trump-backed nationalist. That reflects a broader struggle. ... Battles have raged over divisive issues like migration, abortion, and LGBT rights. ... No longer united by faith in a single model, Poland and other countries on the European Union's eastern flank now find themselves caught between the populist nationalism of Mr. Trump and defenders of the old post-Cold War liberal order.}}</ref> In both countries, higher educational attainment corresponded to higher support for the liberal candidate.<ref>{{cite news|date=November 6, 2024|title=Exit poll results 2024|url=https://www.cnn.com/election/2024/exit-polls/national-results/general/president/0|access-date=November 6, 2024|publisher=CNN|archive-date=November 5, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241105154934/https://www.cnn.com/election/2024/exit-polls/national-results/general/president/0|url-status=live}}</ref>  Like in Poland, where Nawrocki won among working class voters,<ref name="ExitPoll2"/> Trump won low-income voters, while Harris won voters making over $100,000 a year.<ref name="Well-to-Do">{{Cite web|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/10/23/opinion/democrats-rich-poor.html|quote=By 2024, the realignment of income and political party was complete. Americans with more money voted for Kamala Harris while Donald Trump won among the working class.|date=October 23, 2025|access-date=October 23, 2025|title=How Democrats Became the Party of the Well-to-Do|website=The New York Times|first1=Brody|last1=Williams}}</ref>

== Aftermath ==
[[File:Karol Nawrocki speaking after being sworn in on 6 August 2025.jpg|thumb|350px|Karol Nawrocki giving a speech at his inauguration on 6 August 2025]]
Trzaskowski initially claimed victory after the first exit poll showed him leading, while Nawrocki said that the results were too close to call.<ref name=BBC>{{cite web |date={{date|2025-06-02|DMY}} |title=Conservative historian wins Polish presidential vote |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cx27897vedno |publisher=BBC News |access-date=2025-06-02}}</ref> Trzaskowski subsequently conceded after the final results showed Nawrocki winning.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://apnews.com/article/poland-presidential-election-karol-nawrocki-80a99eeb7a2f3ae64260a9263e7028ee |title=Conservative Karol Nawrocki wins Poland's presidential election |publisher=AP News |date=2 June 2025 |access-date=2 June 2025}}</ref> Nawrocki was sworn in on 6 August 2025.

Prime Minister [[Donald Tusk]] called a [[vote of confidence]] on his government, which was held on 11 June.<ref name=BBC/><ref>{{cite web |date={{date|2025-06-03|DMY}} |title=Polish lawmakers to hold confidence vote in Tusk government on June 11 |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/europe/polish-parliament-speaker-says-confidence-vote-should-be-next-week-2025-06-03/ |publisher=Reuters |access-date=2025-06-07}}</ref> Despite speculation of a possible breakdown of the coalition, Tusk survived after gaining the support of all 243 MPs that made up his coalition.<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-06-11|DMY}} |title=Polish PM wins confidence vote but faces rising opposition from coalition allies |url=https://tvpworld.com/87219926/polish-pm-donald-tusk-wins-confidence-vote-but-faces-rising-opposition-from-coalition-allies |work=TVP World |access-date=2025-06-11}}</ref> Later, [[Third Cabinet of Donald Tusk|Donald Tusk's cabinet]] was reshuffled.<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-07-23|DMY}} |title=Donald Tusk zdecydował. Premier wymienia ministrów w swoim rządzie |url=https://www.onet.pl/informacje/onetwiadomosci/rekonstrukcja-rzadu-2025-premier-donald-tusk-wymienia-ministrow-lista/5pvtbyw,79cfc278 |access-date=2025-07-25}}</ref>

The [[Third Way (Poland)|Third Way]] alliance dissolved on 17 June, as the [[Polish People's Party]] declared it will contest the [[next Polish parliamentary election]] separately from [[Szymon Hołownia]]'s [[Poland 2050]].<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-06-17|DMY}} |title=Koniec Trzeciej Drogi |url=https://tvn24.pl/polska/koniec-trzeciej-drogi-st8516654 |access-date=2025-06-17}}</ref> After further disputes within Poland 2050, the party further fractured with half of its parliamentary representation leaving to form [[Centre (Polish parliamentary group)|Centre]] in February 2026.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://wyborcza.pl/7,75398,32607395,grupa-parlamentarzystow-odchodzi-z-polski-2050-to-moment.html |website=[[Gazeta Wyborcza]] |title=Grupa parlamentarzystów odchodzi z Polski 2050. Powstanie klub Centrum |date=18 February 2026 |language=pl |first1=Iwona |last1=Szpala |first2=Agata |last2=Kondzińska}}</ref> Trzaskowski's defeat also led to the creation of the [[New Poland]] and [[New Wave (Polish political party)|New Wave]] parties.<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-09-19|DMY}} |last=Ferfecki |first=Wiktor |title=Nowe partie chcą mieć posłów w Sejmie. Joanna Senyszyn i Wadim Tyszkiewicz wchodzą do gry |url=https://www.rp.pl/polityka/art43033021-nowe-partie-chca-miec-poslow-w-sejmie-joanna-senyszyn-i-wadim-tyszkiewicz-wchodza-do-gry |work=[[Rzeczpospolita (newspaper)|Rzeczpospolita]] |access-date=2025-09-20}}</ref>

=== Election result disputes ===
Several politicians and journalists aligned with the ruling coalition [[election denial|sowed doubt]] about the election results.<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-06-06|DMY}} |title=Silni razem i KO grają narracją o "sfałszowanych" wyborach. Ich tezy nie wytrzymują konfrontacji z realiami |url=https://niezalezna.pl/polska/silni-razem-i-ko-graja-narracja-o-sfalszowanych-wyborach-ich-tezy-nie-wytrzymuja-konfrontacji-z-realiami/545197 |access-date=2025-06-08}}</ref> [[Roman Giertych]] claimed opposition committed organized [[electoral fraud]],<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-06-05|DMY}} |title=Roman Giertych szukał i się doszukał? Poruszy ABW i SN, aby tylko podważyć wynik wyborów |url=https://wpolsce24.tv/polska/roman-giertych-podwaza-wynik-wyborow,34287 |access-date=2025-06-05}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-06-08|DMY}} |title=Giertych twierdzi, że PiS sfałszowało wybory. Czarnek odpowiada kąśliwym cytatem |url=https://dorzeczy.pl/opinie/737973/giertych-twierdzi-ze-pis-sfalszowalo-wybory-czarnek-odpowiada.html |access-date=2025-06-08}}</ref> claiming also that Nawrocki's campaign was advantaged by a right-leaning [[TikTok]] algorithm, which helped them in the campaign.<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-06-05|DMY}} |last=Waluszko |first=Filip |title=Wygrana Karola Nawrockiego w wyborach. Roman Giertych składa zawiadomienie do ABW |url=https://businessinsider.com.pl/wiadomosci/wygrana-karola-nawrockiego-w-wyborach-roman-giertych-sklada-zawiadomienie-do-abw/lpj8nwm |access-date=2025-06-05}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-06-18|DMY}} |last=Wróblewski |first=Michał |title=Sfałszowane wybory? Socjolog nie pozostawia złudzeń. "Kompletna paranoja"  |url=https://wiadomosci.wp.pl/sfalszowane-wybory-socjolog-nie-pozostawia-zludzen-kompletna-paranoja-7169020391050144a |access-date=2025-06-22}}</ref> Many other journalists and politicians, like PKW member [[Ryszard Kalisz]],<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-06-08|DMY}} |title=Kalisz dołącza do chóru "silnych razem". Pod hasłem "liczenia głosów" - próba wywołania chaosu w państwie |url=https://niezalezna.pl/polska/kalisz-dolacza-do-choru-silnych-razem-pod-haslem-liczenia-glosow-proba-wywolania-chaosu-w-panstwie/545285 |access-date=2025-06-08}}</ref> called for a recount of the election. Other figures, like Prime Minister Donald Tusk<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-06-21|DMY}} |last=Pakuła |first=Dagmara |title=Tusk z pytaniem do Dudy, Nawrockiego i Kaczyńskiego. Chodzi o wyniki wyborów |url=https://wydarzenia.interia.pl/wybory/prezydenckie/news-tusk-z-pytaniem-do-dudy-nawrockiego-i-kaczynskiego-chodzi-o,nId,21842992 |access-date=2025-06-22}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-06-20|DMY}} |last=Szczęśniak |first=Agata |title=Tusk: "Wybory nie będą ważne z punktu widzenia wyborców, jeśli nie wyjaśnimy tych wątpliwości" |url=https://oko.press/tusk-wybory-nie-beda-wazne-z-punktu-widzenia-wyborcow |access-date=2025-06-22}}</ref> and Trzaskowski's chief of staff<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-06-06|DMY}} |title=Przemysław Czarnek odpowiada szefowej sztabu Rafała Trzaskowskiego. "Jeden szkopuł" |url=https://www.onet.pl/informacje/onetwiadomosci/anomalie-w-komisjach-czarnek-odpowiada-sztabowi-ko-jeden-szkopul/y7gpv2n,79cfc278 |access-date=2025-06-08}}</ref> or organizations like the Conference of Ambassadors<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-07-01|DMY}} |title=Konferencja ambasadorów miesza! Żądają, by Hołownia nie zwoływał Zgromadzenia Narodowego. "Dziś wzywają do zamachu stanu" |url=https://wpolityce.pl/polityka/733913-zamach-stanu-konferencja-ambasadorow-podwaza-wynik-wyborow |access-date=2025-07-25}}</ref> and [[Committee for the Defence of Democracy]]<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-07-01|DMY}} |title=KOD i zwolennicy Nawrockiego demonstrowali przed Sądem Najwyższym |url=https://tvn24.pl/tvnwarszawa/srodmiescie/wybory-2025-rozstrzygali-o-waznosci-wyborow-protest-przed-sadem-najwyzszym-st8536935 |access-date=2025-07-25}}</ref> also cast doubt on the election results.

According to an SW Research poll for ''[[Rzeczpospolita (newspaper)|Rzeczpospolita]]'' from 17–18 June, 49% of the respondents supported a complete recount of the election.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://wydarzenia.interia.pl/wybory/prezydenckie/news-zapytali-polakow-czy-chca-ponownego-przeliczenia-glosow-poja,nId,21842995 |title=Zapytali Polaków, czy chcą ponownego przeliczenia głosów. Pojawił się sondaż |first=Anna |last=Nicz |date=21 June 2025 |website=[[Interia]] |language=pl}}</ref> However, {{ill|Krzysztof Wiak|pl}}, the President of the Supreme Court, declared that there is no legal basis for a complete recount of the election, as the recount can only be ruled in stations where irregularities occurred.<ref name="dorzeczy_rig">{{cite web |url=https://dorzeczy.pl/kraj/743742/ponowne-przeliczenie-glosow-prezes-sn-mowi-wprost.html |title=Ponowne przeliczenie głosów? Prezes SN mówi wprost |first=Anna |last=Skalska |date=21 June 2025 |language=pl |website=[[Do Rzeczy]]}}</ref>

Following the election, opponents of Nawrocki—including Prime Minister Donald Tusk<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-07-12|DMY}} |last=Rymaszewska |first=Adrianna |title=Hołownia miał postawić się Tuskowi. "Bardzo poważna sprawa" |url=https://wydarzenia.interia.pl/kraj/news-holownia-mial-postawic-sie-tuskowi-bardzo-powazna-sprawa,nId,22164689 |access-date=2025-07-16}}</ref> together with election denialists—attempted to have the [[Marshal of the Sejm]], [[Szymon Hołownia]], block or postpone the inauguration of Karol Nawrocki as president of Poland by calling an indefinite break during the [[National Assembly (Poland)|National Assembly]] (the joint session of the [[Sejm]] and [[Senate of Poland|Senat]]), during Nawrocki's inauguration, after which the Marshal of the Sejm would serve as [[Acting President of Poland|acting president]],<ref name=zamach>{{bulletlist|{{cite news |date={{date|2025-07-25|DMY}} |last=Płatek |first=Karol |title=Szokujące słowa Hołowni. "Proponowano mi zamach stanu. Ujawnię nazwiska |url=https://wiadomosci.radiozet.pl/polityka/szokujace-slowa-holowni-proponowano-mi-zamach-stanu-ujawnie-nazwiska |access-date=2025-07-25}}|{{cite news |date={{date|2025-07-25|DMY}} |last=Makarewicz |first=Nicole |title=Mocne słowa Hołowni: Sugerowano mi zamach stanu |url=https://www.rmf24.pl/polityka/news-mocne-slowa-holowni-sugerowano-mi-zamach-stanu,nId,8003979 |access-date=2025-07-25}}|{{cite news |date={{date|2025-07-25|DMY}} |last=Barański |first=Wojciech |title=Szymon Hołownia: Wielokrotnie sugerowano mi przeprowadzenie zamachu stanu |url=https://www.polsatnews.pl/wiadomosc/2025-07-25/szymon-holownia-wielokrotnie-sugerowano-mi-przeprowadzenie-zamachu-stanu/ |access-date=2025-07-25}}|{{cite news |date={{date|2025-07-25|DMY}} |last=Jaworski |first=Kamil |title=Szymon Hołownia o zamachu stanu. Szokujące, co ujawnił. "Proponowano mi" |url=https://www.fakt.pl/polityka/szymon-holownia-o-zamachu-stanu-proponowano-mi/4g5wmyp |access-date=2025-07-25}}}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-06-24|DMY}} |title=Giertych chce przerwy, Hołownia mu odpowiada. "Jestem z uśmiechem krytyczny" |url=https://www.polsatnews.pl/wiadomosc/2025-06-24/roman-giertych-szymon-holownia-jestem-z-usmiechem-krytyczny/ |access-date=2025-07-14}}</ref> which was described by some as an attempt to conduct a [[coup d'état]].<ref name=zamach/><ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-07-25|DMY}} |last=Kalinowska-Bartosewicz |first=Dorota |title=Tusk planował "zamach stanu"? "Polityczna libacja na skwerku" |url=https://www.tokfm.pl/Tokfm/7,103087,32110027,tusk-planowal-zamach-stanu-polityczna-libacja-na-skwerku.html |access-date=2025-07-25}}</ref> Following Hołownia's refusal of the idea, pro-government outlets like ''[[Gazeta Wyborcza]]'' accused Hołownia of treason against the [[Constitution of Poland|Constitution]].<ref>{{cite news |date={{date|2025-06-30|DMY}} |title=Marszałek Sejmu chce złamać Konstytucję, a więc przyczynić się do demontażu demokracji |url=https://wyborcza.pl/7,162657,32066517,marszalek-sejmu-chce-zlamac-konstytucje-a-wiec-przyczynic-sie.html |access-date=2025-07-14}}</ref>

